  "description": "RAMZEM crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H114 Dy9 N24 O50 1+,H1 O1 1-,1.6(H2 O1),0.6(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1C (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3C (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.542-5.059 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.44-177.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(OH)10(hmp)8(NO3)8(DMF)8](OH)·1.6H2O·0.6CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
